Waycar patch for libssh2 c7557852f1b7c0d3b9cffd5390eb33fdf93fb17f.

channel: pipelined channel opens

ssh2_channel_open() keeps an unfinished open in session state (open_state,
open_channel, open_packet, open_data, open_packet_requirev_state, and
direct_state/direct_message for direct-tcpip and direct-streamlocal), so a
second open entered during the first one's EAGAIN would resume the first:
only one open can be in flight per session.

New libssh2_channel_open_start(), libssh2_channel_direct_tcpip_start() and
libssh2_channel_direct_streamlocal_start() allocate the channel, register
it, and build its CHANNEL_OPEN request in per-channel state (openNB_*)
without any I/O. libssh2_channel_open_finish() sends that request and
waits for the reply matching this channel's local id only, so any number
of opens can await their replies at once. Stock opens are untouched and
can interleave with pipelined ones.

A refused or failed open is marked closed locally; libssh2_channel_free()
still owns releasing it. Freeing an open the server may have seen (fully
sent, or partially held by the transport) first waits for its reply and
then sends the ordinary CHANNEL_CLOSE if it was confirmed, so no channel
is left open on the server; an open never handed to the transport is just
discarded. libssh2_channel_close() refuses a channel whose open has not
completed, since it has no remote id yet.

