+/* Waycar patch: pipelined channel opens. The stock open functions keep an
+   unfinished open in session state, so only one can be in flight. The
+   *_start() functions only build the CHANNEL_OPEN request (no I/O) and return
+   the channel, or NULL on bad input or allocation failure.
+   libssh2_channel_open_finish() sends that request and waits for this
+   channel's reply only; non-blocking callers repeat it while it returns
+   LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN, so several opens can await their replies at once.
+   It returns 0 once the server confirmed (and for any channel that is not a
+   pending pipelined open); a refusal returns LIBSSH2_ERROR_CHANNEL_FAILURE
+   with the reason in the last error message. Until it has returned 0, call
+   only libssh2_channel_open_finish() and libssh2_channel_free() on the
+   channel. Every started channel, refused ones included, must be freed with
+   libssh2_channel_free(); freeing an open the server may already have seen
+   first waits for its reply, then closes it if it was confirmed.
+   A request the transport holds partially sent blocks every other send
+   until its own libssh2_channel_open_finish() (or free) resumes it. */
